  "summary": "After Dayton, Minnesota's city council voted on August 25 to suspend its ALPR program and cancel its Flock contract over privacy concerns, Flock allegedly reinstalled two cameras in September without authorization. The city posted on Facebook that it had told Flock the program was on hold and ordered the Dayton Police Department to remove the newly reinstalled cameras.",
  "key_quotes": [
